      "title": "‘We expected it, but now it’s here’: on the frontline of Australia’s bird flu outbreak, people are distressed",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/07/we-expected-it-but-now-its-here-on-the-frontline-of-australias-bird-flu-outbreak-people-are-distressed",
      "description": "<p>As Australia prepares for the H5 bird flu to potentially rip through hundreds of species, residents of the Limestone Coast are already seeing the impacts</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/07/royal-commission-antisemitism-national-cabinet-datacentres-icac-liberal-party-labor-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>It has only been three weeks since <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/01/first-australian-mass-mortality-event-suspected-as-deadly-bird-flu-virus-rapidly-escalates-among-native-birds\">H5 bird flu was detected</a> on South Australia’s Limestone Coast and already encounters with sick or dead birds are becoming commonplace.</p><p>Maureen Christie, who lives in the seaside town of Carpenter Rocks, has been observing and protecting birds in the region for decades. She is now witnessing many stricken and suffering.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/07/we-expected-it-but-now-its-here-on-the-frontline-of-australias-bird-flu-outbreak-people-are-distressed\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-06T15:00:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "Minns said he wouldn’t ‘gloat’ about Icac hearings into the Liberals. Instead, he’s quietly taking out the trash",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/07/minns-said-he-wouldnt-gloat-about-icac-hearings-into-the-liberals-instead-hes-quietly-taken-out-the-trash",
      "description": "<p>Amid revelations that could damage the opposition’s state election hopes, the NSW government dropped key documents on three contentious issues</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/07/royal-commission-antisemitism-national-cabinet-datacentres-icac-liberal-party-labor-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-angus-taylor-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>During the first week of the Independent Commission Against Corruption’s Operation Rosny’s <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/06/jean-claude-perrottet-icac-angus-taylor-reformers-ntwnfb\">hearings into allegations</a> against people associated with the New South Wales Liberal party, Chris Minns took the high ground.</p><p>“There’ll be no gloating or taking political advantage,” the NSW Labor premier told reporters. “It’s an important process and ultimately, hopefully, it makes all political parties cleaner and sends a message to anyone who’s thinking of breaching the laws or committing a corrupt act, that someone is watching.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/07/minns-said-he-wouldnt-gloat-about-icac-hearings-into-the-liberals-instead-hes-quietly-taken-out-the-trash\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-06T15:00:05"
    },
